From: mscharged-port
Subject: Admit the original Road to Striker Cup setup, hub and detail pages
Upstream-base: efa6fc84680e48bfdca7e6ac245d8abf333ae617
Classification: temporary explicit original-source diagnostic admission; depends on 0505, 0571 and 0600.

Main Menu's cup item (SHMainMenu item 2) starts a new cup through StartNewCup
or offers ContinueStrikerCup/ShowNewCupPrompt; feCupFlow and CupManager own
every decision and save request. The authored transitions push the Striker Cup
captain and sidekick setup (scenes 6/7), the cup news (39) and the hub (31).
The hub's Schedule, Cup Stats, Rules and Play buttons reach the group schedule
(32), standings and award pages (36-38), the original rules popup and the Cup
Choose Sides (8).

Under the named MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_CUP admission, move those factory
cases and the three FE presentation natives the cup transitions call (24: cup
camera by mode, 26: push Cup Choose Sides, 39: rules popup) into the admitted
set, splitting gated blocks only at case boundaries. Cup cheat (9), game
results (33), knockout/final round pages (34/35), the award and forfeit natives
(4, 37, 38, 40) keep their gates. Allocation, constructors and case bodies are
unchanged.

The hub, standings and awards handlers read their pointer-button index from the
callback context word; natively it is a pointer-width value narrowed through
std::uintptr_t. Console builds keep the literal casts.

